{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790970364,"nonce":"inU5oo208Gn/IUS0oMplIyIjgBE=","message":"It has now run in a browser: Ash's page in headless Chrome at a device scale of 2, with Ash d19312b41993d0b2bf909d76f28d40783c4cf869 (local, not pushed), which loads side modules in the page. The program opened the window and read its size, scale, focus and title. It set the title, a cursor icon, a cursor image and IME, and asked for a redraw. Then it took a click, the wheel, a, Shift-B and the left arrow, closed the window and exited 0. The page showed the new title and the blob cursor.\n\nThe run found three agent defects, fixed in the working tree with page_agent covering each:\n\n- Window.open could return the canvas's page size, not the size it asked for. The agent posted the starting size before serving the mailbox, and open took the first size it saw. A size command now posts the size it lays out to.\n- The first key posted a ModifiersChanged with nothing held.\n- A wheel axis that did not move read -0.\n\nNot exercised: pointer lock and fullscreen waiting for input, file drops, a real input method, and a GPU drawing to the canvas.\n\nUse Chrome's --force-device-scale-factor to test scale, not CDP's Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride. Under emulation, devicePixelRatio follows the override but ResizeObserver's devicePixelContentBoxSize does not, so sizes look half as large.","files":null}]}